m/users/dav-is/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dav-is/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think the imports should be directly above their usage. For types, it should be right under the `API Reference` title","created_at":"2026-03-26T23:49:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T23:50:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998289689","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998289689"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998289689"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998289689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":14,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":14,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998537213","pull_request_review_id":4018371243,"id":2998537213,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOLW-eZs6yugv9","diff_hunk":"","path":"packages/react/src/otp-field/root/OTPFieldRoot.tsx","commit_id":"62086e3177d5c56f90e9a6a4ef36f7757249ec9a","original_commit_id":"3c5ec66c52f340b4c1c8bf7a0d90915715d80270","user":{"login":"romgrk","id":1423607,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjM2MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1423607?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk","html_url":"https://github.com/romgrk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Coming in late and I haven't followed the discussions, but did you consider implementing the OTP field as a single input instead of multiple ones? It has a lot of performance, bundle-size, maintainability & accessibility benefits.","created_at":"2026-03-27T01:38:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T01:38:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998537213","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998537213"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998537213"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998537213/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998770294","pull_request_review_id":4018639967,"id":2998770294,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOLW-eZs6yvZp2","diff_hunk":"","path":"packages/react/src/otp-field/root/OTPFieldRoot.tsx","commit_id":"62086e3177d5c56f90e9a6a4ef36f7757249ec9a","original_commit_id":"3c5ec66c52f340b4c1c8bf7a0d90915715d80270","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fair question to ask. The current implementation is basically the status quo across the major libraries (Radix, Ark, Mantine). The odd one out (actually what shadcn happens to use) is `input-otp` but I'm not convinced it's a good idea.\n\n### Maintainability\n\nThe most popular implementation of the real input idea appears to have some bugs that this PR's doesn't right now — it seems like syncing the input's state to real visual inputs is actually more challenging than just using real ones just from a basic first user experience glance.\n\n(I know this isn’t proof of better or worse maintainability, but without redesigning the API around a single-input model just to validate that claim, I think it’s reasonable to treat a popular, battle-tested implementation as evidence that this approach also carries meaningful complexity in practice.)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/01ee0001-3e78-478f-a74c-8f1052c17c40\n\nFrom Codex: \n\n\"The strongest single-input-specific issues I found in `input-otp` are:\n\n- Password manager badge overlap.\n  The overlaid real input can end up with 1Password-style save/fill badges covering the last visible slot.\n\n- Password manager autofill quirks.\n  There are reports of some managers, like Dashlane, not filling 2FA correctly.\n\n- Hidden-input width/layout hacks.\n  The invisible absolute input uses width expansion tricks, which has led to overflow and layout-shift issues.\n\n- Caret/selection artifacts on iOS.\n  Because there is still one real input underneath, its caret/selection can leak through visually on mobile Safari/iOS.\n\n- Clicking a visual slot maps to the wrong logical position.\n  Translating a click on a fake slot back into the correct selection/caret position in one real input turns out to be surprisingly tricky, and there are multiple reports around that.\n\n- Visual focus not matching actual typing focus.\n  There are cases where the component still appears focused after programmatic resets, but typing no longer works until the user clicks again.\n\n- Extra CSS/runtime plumbing for autofill styling.\n  The architecture needs more special handling around the real hidden/overlay input, which has led to CSS injection, CSP, and WebView-specific issues.\n\nThe best piece of evidence is actually the maintainer’s own “limitations/issues caused by core implementation” note, which explicitly calls out architecture-driven downsides like:\n- visible iOS selection artifacts\n- inability to truly click/touch-select arbitrary slots\n\nSo the maintainability point I’d make is:\n\nI’m also not convinced the maintainability advantage is as clear-cut as it sounds. The single-input model clearly works, but it also seems to introduce its own architecture-specific complexity around the overlaid native input: password-manager interactions, width/layout hacks, iOS caret/selection artifacts, and mapping clicks on visual slots back to one real input. I don’t think that proves the model is worse, but it does suggest the tradeoff is more “different complexity” than “obviously simpler to maintain.”\n- compressed-letter/caret hacks needed to make the illusion work\"\n\n### Performance\n\nThis as far as I'm concerned is not relevant, because OTP fields won't be rendered more than once on a single page in 99% of scenarios — I cannot imagine why they would be. \n\nBut based on local bechmarks, it doesn't seem like it brings a benefit anyway:\n\n| Benchmark | Base UI OTPField | input-otp | Relative result |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| Repeated mount/unmount 1,000x | 775 ms | 1164 ms | Base UI ~1.50x faster |\n| Repeated mount/unmount per instance | 0.775 ms | 1.164 ms | Base UI ~1.50x faster |\n| Bulk mount 1,000 instances | 649 ms | 639 ms | Roughly tied |\n| Bulk mount per instance | 0.649 ms | 0.639 ms | Roughly tied |\n| DOM elements per instance | 8 | 11 | Base UI renders fewer elements |\n\n(Again, have to defer to an existing solution for this claim - it's not proof on its own)\n\n### Accessibility\n\nThis is the strongest concern, but my hunch is that it's not a clear issue. \n\nPlaying around with VoiceOver myself on this comp reads just like it visually appears: \"_Character 1 of 6, edit text, Verification code, Enter the 6 character code we sent to your device, group_\". This indicates it's a grouped composite widget that has input-like keyboard interactions with individual digit slots quite clearly. The one on the shadcn page is more like a real input field but honestly that seems less like a plainly obvious \"this is a 6-digit code with individual slots\" widget. Additionally, VoiceOver's virtual cursor appears misplaced with the shadcn one while ours correctly highlights the correct slot.\n\nEdit: After testing NVDA, JAWS, and Narrator on Windows, all have similar semantics to macOS VoiceOver and all make coherent sense regarding what the component does/requires of users. So the multi-input model seems to be AT accessible.","created_at":"2026-03-27T03:19:50Z","updated_at":"2026-04-07T07:53:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998770294","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998770294"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4365#discussion_r2998770294"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4365"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/2998770294/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2998537213,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/comments/3030766334","pull_request_review_id":4053607417,"id":3030766334,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOLW-eZs60pdL-","diff_hunk":"","path":"packages/react/src/otp-field/root/OTPFieldRoot.tsx","commit_id":"62086e3177d5c56f90e9a6a4ef36f7757249ec9a","original_commit_id":"3c5ec66c52f340b4c1c8bf7a0d90915715d80270","user":{"login":"romgrk","id":1423607,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjM2MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1423607?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk","html_url":"https://github.com/romgrk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgrk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"h